{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-25T00:09:23.381Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"74cfeef4f534f3b98c3259d0","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Observed\n\nExtensions keep their configuration in their own section of `.agents/pm/settings.json` (for example `\"lint\": {...}`, `\"jev\": {...}`). The public SDK has `readSettings` / `readSettingsWithMetadata`, which validate and return the normalized core `PmSettings` tree and strip extension-owned keys. There is no supported way to read an extension's own section: `readSettingsSection` / `readWorkspaceSettingsSection` (or an equivalent) do not exist in 2026.10.24's exports (checked: every export matching /setting|config/ is `CONFIG_FLAG_CONTRACTS SETTINGS_DEFAULTS config getSettingsPath readSettings readSettingsWithMetadata resolveConfiguredPmPackageRoot resolveSettingsWithSemanticRuntimeDefaults runConfig runWithConfigurationOnlySettings writeSettings`).\n\nSo packages call `readSettings()` only to validate, then re-read and `JSON.parse` the file themselves via `getSettingsPath()`:\n\n- pm-lint `src/settings.ts`: `await readSettings(pmRoot); // SDK readSettings validates core settings but strips extension-owned keys.` followed by a raw file read and its own \"settings disappeared during read\" race handling.\n- pm-jev `index.ts` and `decision-calibration.ts` do the same.\n\nThat bypasses the host's backend abstraction: on a non-filesystem backend (hosted Postgres, remote MCP) there is no settings file path, so the extension's configuration silently disappears. It also duplicates parsing, error handling and race handling in every package.\n\n## Expected\n\nA host-bound reader for an extension's own section, for example:\n\n```ts\nconst section = await readSettingsSection(pmRoot, 'lint', { validate: lintSettingsSchema.parse });\n// -> { value, source: 'file' | 'default' | 'backend', revision } or a typed refusal (missing / malformed / backend-unsupported)\n```\n\nThe same reader should be available on the extension command context. Malformed sections should produce a typed refusal with a remedy rather than a thrown `JSON.parse` error, and it should work through whatever backend the host is bound to. A matching `writeSettingsSection` with an expected revision would complete it.\n\n## Why it matters for agents\n\nAgents configure extensions per tracker. Today an extension's settings work only when the tracker is a local directory, and every package re-implements a fragile raw read. Reading through the SDK would make extension configuration backend-neutral and remove the duplicated code.\n\nVersion: `@unbrained/pm-cli` 2026.10.24."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1580"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1580: Host-bound extension settings sections"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"SDK: no supported reader for an extension's own settings section, so packages re-read settings.json by path and lose their configuration on non-filesystem backends"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["configuration","extensions","gh:1580","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-25T00:09:23.381Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-25T00:09:23.381Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"SDK-owned settings-section read and revision-safe write primitives on host-bound extension contexts; backend-neutral capability/refusal contracts; avoid direct settings.json reads."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-9rgaal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-25T00:09:23.381Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Intake source: 1580. Duplicate check: complete strict 3101-item all-status corpus with no omissions, request-specific searches and current open/in_progress lists; related delivered lineage retained. Report recorded for independent verification. No implementation or completion claimed by intake."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"35284cd589155641bdb5eafe31948f4b86e561a4a6526e3d94af24d4ee7d9fa6","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"947a0b704c6e0a09ffd8b9d0d53098db2a90e961459efe4def9dff36be96f9dd"}
