{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T11:09:04.697Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489489c9e2938b0738fed20a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-4zpq71","claim:pm-fr10t8","claim:pm-gh1580","claim:pm-gh1647","lineage:pm-fr10t8","lineage:pm-yql1","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-4zpq71+pm-fr10t8+pm-gh1580+pm-gh1647","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-4zpq71","claim:pm-fr10t8","claim:pm-gh1580","claim:pm-gh1647","lineage:pm-fr10t8","lineage:pm-yql1","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-01T11:09:04.697Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation: new src/core/store/settings-sections.ts. readSettingsSection(pmRoot, section, { validate, defaultValue }) returns { section, source: \"stored\" | \"default\", value, revision }. The revision is \"sha256:<hex>\" of the stable-stringified stored value, or null when the section is absent. writeSettingsSection(pmRoot, section, value | undefined, { expectedRevision, validate }) replaces or removes the section under the workspace-history lock, appends one settings:section:write event, keeps every other key, writes nothing for an unchanged value, and makes the write compare-and-set when expectedRevision is given (null requires absence). Typed refusals: settings_section_name_invalid and settings_section_reserved (the core keys come from the new CORE_SETTINGS_SECTION_KEYS, derived from the validator shape so they cannot drift), settings_section_document_malformed (reason settings_json_malformed or settings_json_not_object, instead of a thrown JSON.parse error), settings_section_invalid (validator throw, bounded message; also values JSON cannot represent), settings_section_revision_conflict (exit 4, with expected_revision and current_revision added to PmCliErrorContext), and settings_section_document_missing (exit 3). Both functions and settingsSectionRevision are public SDK exports through runtime-primitives. ExtensionCommandSdk gains readSettingsSection and writeSettingsSection bound to the invocation tracker, so a package using context.sdk inherits any future settings backend; the backend abstraction itself stays with pm-gh1399. Docs: new section in docs/SDK_CONFIGURATION_SAFETY.md. Tests: tests/unit/core/store/settings-sections.spec.ts, 16 cases, 100% branch coverage of the module.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T11:09:04.697Z"}],"before_hash":"0c771fba9c35cee035c2267aa9baee58d8ac58d07ee17afd6f4c11558bb2800c","after_hash":"1eb78fc64704ab579aa46cbee8ba7a10eb24837179dc9452719c0e017599882f","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"9077ba6ada386f1ac919ccec9b5832b17890e42564d98e2e7e522c6e6fd413f2"}
